      "seed": 772776877,
      "version": 1312,
      "versionNonce": 289851939,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1774632734073,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4. Two hundred factory machines generate sensor\nreadings every 500 milliseconds. Five billion events\nper day. All streaming into ADLS Gen2 via Event\nHubs Capture. The folder structure must support\ntime-series queries and partition pruning in Spark —\notherwise querying last week's data scans the\nentire history",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4. Two hundred factory machines generate sensor readings every 500 milliseconds. Five billion events per day. All streaming into ADLS Gen2 via Event Hubs Capture. The folder structure must support time-series queries and partition pruning in Spark — otherwise querying last week's data scans the entire history",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
