      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Familiar object storage model. \n- No POSIX ACL management. \n- Cost: slightly lower — same base price, slightly lower transaction cost. \n- Scalability: same at rest. \n- Directory operations are slower because there is no B-tree metadata layer. \n- Maintenance: higher for anyone doing analytical workloads — no atomic rename\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Familiar object storage model. \n- No POSIX ACL management. \n- Cost: slightly lower — same base price, slightly lower transaction cost. \n- Scalability: same at rest. \n- Directory operations are slower because there is no B-tree metadata layer. \n- Maintenance: higher for anyone doing analytical workloads — no atomic rename\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "uC_Xox7-szgh8cXvyR610",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 254.3498239544921,
      "y": 9047.008305042522,
      "width": 1299.99951171875,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1p",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2084896742,
      "version": 544,
      "versionNonce": 1309822310,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1774672999438,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. Databricks DBFS  -                       - DBFS is managed by Databricks and auto-mounted. \n                                                   - Cost: higher — Databricks cluster overhead applies, \n                                                   - DBFS root is actually backed by Azure Blob Storage internally, \n                                                        so you get neither the benefits of Gen2 nor the cost savings of direct Blob Storage. \n                                                   - Scalability: limited — data is tied to the Databricks workspace. \n                                                        workspace gone -   data gone. \n                                                   - Maintenance: data is not accessible outside the Databricks workspace without explicit \n                                                    external location configurations \n                                                    \n3 Snowfalke on Azure -                      query engine not lake\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2. Databricks DBFS  -                       - DBFS is managed by Databricks and auto-mounted. \n                                                   - Cost: higher — Databricks cluster overhead applies, \n                                                   - DBFS root is actually backed by Azure Blob Storage internally, \n                                                        so you get neither the benefits of Gen2 nor the cost savings of direct Blob Storage. \n                                                   - Scalability: limited — data is tied to the Databricks workspace. \n                                                        workspace gone -   data gone. \n                                                   - Maintenance: data is not accessible outside the Databricks workspace without explicit \n                                                    external location configurations \n                                                    \n3 Snowfalke on Azure -                      query engine not lake\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
